  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Amino acids contain amino (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>) and carboxyl (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math>) functional groups.&nbsp;Depending upon the relative position of the amino group with respect to the carboxyl group, the amino acids can be classified as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#948;</mi></math>&nbsp;and so on. Only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>amino acids are obtained on the hydrolysis of proteins.&nbsp;</p><p>So, only in option (B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>-amino acid given all the other options are not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>-amino acids.</p>"
